0,Miao people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miao_people,"Following the communist takeover of Laos in 1975, a large group of Hmong refugees resettled in several Western nations, mainly in the United States, France, and Australia. Miao is a Chinese term referring to many groups that have their own autonyms such as Hmong, Hmu, Xong (Qo-Xiong), and A-Hmao.","Miao, Eastern Huishui",Hmong-Mien
1,Hmong–Mien languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hmong–Mien_languages,"Meo, Hmu, Mong, Hmao, and Hmong are local names for Miao, but since most Laotian refugees in the United States call themselves Hmong/Mong, this name has become better known in English than the others in recent decades.","Miao, Eastern Huishui",Hmong-Mien
2,West Hmongic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Hmongic_languages,"The West Hmongic languages, also known as Chuanqiandian Miao and Western Miao, are a major branch of the Hmongic languages of China and Southeast Asia.","Miao, Eastern Huishui",Hmong-Mien
3,Miao (Hmong) Music (music genre) | WorldMusic,https://worldmusic.heuron.com/en/genres/miao-music,"The music is tied to agricultural ritual, courtship gatherings, and seasonal festivals. Oral transmission has carried the tradition for over a millennium, and there is no single unified 'Miao musical canon' — each village's repertoire is locally specific.","Miao, Eastern Huishui",Hmong-Mien
4,"Miao People's Ancient Ethnic Song ""Maple Song"" | Chinese ...Hmong/Miao songs - YouTube MusicMiao people - WikipediaHmong–Mien languages - WikipediaTraditional Miao Songs - Smithsonian's National Museum of ...Huishui Miao language explained",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b83_E2mrPCw,"Apr 28, 2024 · Some sub-groups of the Miao, most notably the Hmong people, have migrated out of China into Southeast Asia (Myanmar, Northern Vietnam, Laos, and Thailand). All songs were found on Youtube, all credit goes to their rightful owners and song makers. I do not take any credit. Following the communist takeover of Laos in 1975, a large group of Hmong refugees resettled in several Western nations, mainly in the United States, France, and Australia. Miao is a Chinese term referring to many groups that have their own autonyms such as Hmong, Hmu, Xong (Qo-Xiong), and A-Hmao. Meo, Hmu, Mong, Hmao, and Hmong are local names for Miao, but since most Laotian refugees in the United States call themselves Hmong/Mong, this name has become better known in English than the others in recent decades. Traditionally, Miao music is often accompanied by the lusheng, an instrument consisting of multiple bamboo pipes, a cup-shaped body, and a reed. The lusheng is known as a “talking instrument” because it creates musical tones that mimic the human voice. Below is a list of Miao dialects and their respective speaker populations and distributions from Li (2018), [1] along with representative datapoints from Wang (1985).","Miao, Eastern Huishui",Hmong-Mien
5,Traditional Miao Songs - Smithsonian's National Museum of ...,https://asia-archive.si.edu/learn/for-educators/teaching-china-with-the-smithsonian/videos/traditional-miao-songs/,"Traditionally, Miao music is often accompanied by the lusheng, an instrument consisting of multiple bamboo pipes, a cup-shaped body, and a reed. The lusheng is known as a “talking instrument” because it creates musical tones that mimic the human voice.","Miao, Eastern Huishui",Hmong-Mien
